{"text": "PAUL N. EGBULEFU\nJacksonville, FL\n\nCHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER\n\nVisionary, entrepreneurial, and driven Chief Executive, with 24 years hands-on leadership and\nexpertise in founding and leading numerous companies in domestic and international\nmarketplaces. Passionate about vision, strategy. and operational excellence. Facilitator and\nbuilder of world-class management and service teams in start-up and growth stages. Proven\nfundraising and networking skills Building employees and worldwide partnerships in both for\nprofit and non-profit organizations with demonstrated multi-million dollar bottom line growth.\n\nDemonstrated Achievements\nGrew CHF dba Hope Heritage Foundation revenue from $3 Million to $58 Million,\nand a worldwide professional volunteer network from 700 to 8000 within 6 years.\nBuilt BT Investment Group Inc from a $75,000 company to $42 Million when it\nwas sold in 2003,\nY Founded Center Star Energy LLC with 3 other Co-founders and sold it after three\nyears at a highly profit exit\nY Led Dashen Investment Group Ltd as Senior Consultant in a $4.8 Billion USD real\nestate and hotel acquisitions in North America and Europe respectively.\n\nCore Competencies\n\n\u00a5 Company Management Strategic Oversight Market Insight\nY Budget Management Capital Raising Client Outreach\nY Leadership & Team building Negotiation Public Relations\nEXECUTIVE EXPERIENCE\nCEO: CHF Hope Heritage Foundation, Jacksonville, FL 2011-Present\nCFO: CHF Hope Heritage Foundation 2009-2010,\nCOO: CHF Hope Heritage Foundation 2006-2008\n\nProvide visionary leadership for a multi-million dollar organization with worldwide humanitarian\nProjects\n+ Oversee the effective management of the organization.\n* Determine strategic direction and spearhead cost cutting measures and personnel\nchanges that freed milions of dollars for the organization's programs.\n* Lead long and short term goals in-line with the visions of the Board of Directors.\nImplement fundraising events, and effective applications of corporate resources to\n\u2018accomplish the organizations programs\n* Establish and monitor processes for reaching set goals and compliance of corporate\nprinciples and report back to the Board,\n* Interface with grantors, donors, government agencies and the Board of Directors on\naffairs of the corporation.\n* Participate in major contract negotiation and enforce accountability.\n* Build consensus among managers, directors, contractors, volunteers, employees, and\npublic agencies to attain the organization's program objectives.",
